"use strict";Object.defineProperty(exports,"__esModule",{value:!0}),exports.VUE_ENHANCEMENT_PROMPT=void 0,exports.VUE_ENHANCEMENT_PROMPT="\nYou are a Vue.js expert. Given the generated code and design screenshots,\ncleanup and refactor the code while integrating it into the target project.\n\n## DESIGN SCREENSHOTS\n{screenshots}\n\nUse these screenshots to match the design intent as closely as possible.\n\n## ⚠️ FILE SIZE GUIDELINE\n\n**Target**: Keep files under 300 lines (excluding comments and blank lines) for maintainability.\n\n**Best practice workflow:**\n1. Check source file line counts\n2. For files exceeding 300 lines, consider extracting components\n3. Create an extraction plan when beneficial:\n   - Original file size and logical split points\n   - Components to extract (with estimated line counts)\n   - Target file sizes after extraction\n4. Execute extraction if it improves code organization\n\n**How to extract Vue components:**\n- Identify repeated UI patterns (cards, list items, form sections, headers)\n- Extract template blocks with 10+ elements into separate components\n- Split large pages/views using this pattern:\n  • Header component (navigation, title, actions)\n  • Content sections (main page body split by logical sections)\n  • Footer/BottomBar component (footer, bottom navigation)\n- Move complex logic into composables (separate files)\n- Extract types/interfaces into separate .types.ts files\n- Create utility functions in separate files\n\n**Example extraction plan:**\n```\n📋 EXTRACTION PLAN\n\nOriginal: BookingView.vue (742 lines) ❌ EXCEEDS LIMIT\n\nExtracting:\n  → components/BookingHeader.vue (~50 lines)\n    - Navigation header with back button and notifications\n\n  → components/VehicleTypeCard.vue (~60 lines)\n    - Vehicle selection card component\n\n  → components/ItemTypeCard.vue (~60 lines)\n    - Item type selection card component\n\n  → components/BookingFormSection.vue (~160 lines)\n    - Form fields section (location, date, time)\n\n  → components/BottomNavigation.vue (~75 lines)\n    - Bottom navigation bar with tabs\n\n  → composables/useBookingForm.ts (~90 lines)\n    - Form state management and validation logic\n\n  → types/booking.types.ts (~35 lines)\n    - TypeScript interfaces and types\n\nResult: BookingView.vue (~212 lines) ✅ WITHIN LIMIT\n\nAll extracted files also within limit ✅\n```\n\n## ENHANCEMENT CHECKLIST\n\n### IMPORTANT NOTE\nFor components with comments indicating custom components, DO NOT MODIFY or REMOVE them.\nThey must be preserved in the output code.\n\n### Improve Naming\n- Fix component, prop, and variable names\n- Use descriptive names (not Component1, Data, Item)\n- Use PascalCase for components, camelCase for variables/methods\n- Avoid generic names and number suffixes\n\n### Use Proper Vue Patterns\n- Composition API (script setup) for Vue 3\n- TypeScript for type safety\n- Proper prop definitions with types\n- Emits for component events\n\n### Reactivity and State\n- ref() for primitive reactive values\n- reactive() for objects\n- computed() for derived state\n- watch/watchEffect for side effects\n- Proper reactive destructuring\n\n### Styling Approach\n- Scoped styles: <style scoped>\n- CSS Modules if used in project\n- Tailwind classes if applicable\n- Maintain consistency with existing code\n\n### Template Best Practices\n- Use v-for with :key\n- v-if/v-else-if/v-else for conditionals\n- v-model for two-way binding\n- Event handlers with @click, @input, etc.\n- Slot usage for composition\n\n### Add Functionality\n- Event handlers for interactive elements\n- Form validation\n- Loading and error states\n- Accessibility attributes\n\n### TypeScript Types\n- Define proper interfaces for props\n- Use defineProps with types\n- defineEmits with event types\n- Avoid 'any' type\n\n### Code Quality\n- **Strong preference**: Max 300 lines per file\n- Create extraction plan for oversized files before integration\n- Extract reusable components into separate .vue files when it improves organization\n- Separate concerns (logic in composables, template in components, types in .types.ts) when beneficial\n- Move complex logic to composables (useFeatureName pattern) when it clarifies the code\n- Use meaningful variable names\n\n### Composables\n- Extract reusable logic to composables\n- Use proper naming (useFeatureName)\n- Return reactive values and methods\n- Document usage\n\n### Documentation\n- JSDoc comments for components\n- Explain props, emits, and slots\n- Add usage examples\n\n### Stay Pixel-Perfect\n- Match design exactly\n- Compare with screenshots and preserve spacing, sizing, colors, fonts, alignment\n- Use responsive design patterns\n\n### Code Syntax\n- Fix all syntax errors and ensure code compiles\n- Add necessary imports\n- Ensure correct Vue 3 syntax\n- Use proper TypeScript syntax\n";